    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d529">

                <pb facs="0553" n="541" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg541"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51A/1–1945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-19T18:00:00+03:25">January 19, 1945—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 19—5:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>39. ReEmbs 30, January 17. Bayat has written Millspaugh sharp reply<anchor n="13"
                        xml:id="d529-f1"/> to his letter regarding Ebtehaj dispute. Prime Minister
                    flatly rejects Millspaugh demand that Ebtehaj be removed or at least suspended
                    and suggests that if Millspaugh still insists he should have matter referred to
                    Majlis through Finance Minister.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d529-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>As yet Millspaugh who has been ill for several days has said nothing to me
                    regarding his plans in light of this development.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d529-f1" n="13" xml:id="d529-f1-content">
                <p>Dated January 18. Copy transmitted to the Department by the Ambassador in Iran in
                    despatch 185, January 24, 1945; neither printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d529-f2" n="14" xml:id="d529-f2-content">
                <p>Amanollah Ardalan.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
